{
  "name": "Pulse of the Forge",
  "type": "feat",
  "img": "art/bbttcc/GOTTGAIT/BBTTCC%20Button%20Icons/bbttcc_icons_flame_1.png",
  "system": {
    "category": "technique",
    "source": "Bad Eden (2024 rules)",
    "tags": [],
    "description": {
      "value": "<div data-ft-phase5-vocab-scrub=\"v1\" style=\"display:none\"></div><p><strong>Pulse of the Forge.</strong> You can flare the metaphysical coals inside you and share that heat with others.</p><ul><li><p>Once per short or a Soma Break, as an action, you release a wave of stabilizing heat in a 3 squares radius around you.</p></li><li><p>Choose up to a number of creatures equal to your Body modifier (minimum one) in the area. Each target regains Integrity equal to your <strong>tier + Body modifier</strong>.</p></li><li><p>This does not affect constructs that have no metaphysical presence in your setting (at the GM’s discretion), but it absolutely works on anyone carrying scars, stress, or long nights.</p></li></ul>",
      "chat": ""
    },
